{%- comment -%}
  Florista homepage hero — restyled 2026-08-20 as part of the boho-boutique homepage pass.

  The blurred glass panel from the first build is gone. The owner called the site's look generic —
  "very AI" — and a floating frosted-glass card over a photo is exactly the kind of default the
  frontend-design skill names as a templated AI tell. This version puts the title and CTA
  straight on the photo, editorial-style (reference: examples/ screenshots, an UrbanStems hero —
  large serif-scale type directly on a lifestyle photo, a bottom gradient, no card). Heebo has no
  serif cut and stays the only typeface per CLAUDE.md (Hebrew glyph coverage is an engineering
  constraint, not a style choice available to revisit here) — the editorial feel comes from scale,
  weight and a tracked micro-label instead, not a family swap.

  Full-bleed, full-screen (min-block-size: 100svh below the sticky header). Content sits on the
  physical right — inline-START on this permanently-RTL site — in logical properties throughout.

  Source photo swapped 2026-08-21 (`iimages to use/Beach picnic.jpg`, 2752×1536): golden-hour
  beach, wine and grapes on a blanket beside an oversized bouquet — picked because it directly
  parallels the urbanstems.com reference the owner gave (their own hero is beach + wine + flowers), and
  because it's native landscape so it needs far less crop distortion than the portrait "woman on a
  street" alternative did. No people in frame, unlike that alternative — sidesteps any likeness
  question for a stock/AI-sourced photo entirely. Derivatives: `hero-beach-{640,960,1280,1920}.
  {jpg,webp}`.

  Second pass, same day, the owner's direct feedback: the eyebrow label is gone (was "חיפה · נווה שאנן"
  — that address-level detail already lives in the footer and the SEO section; the hero doesn't
  need to repeat it), content moved from bottom-anchored to vertical-center (was glued to the
  very bottom edge, which read as an afterthought), and the CTA is now solid wine fill instead of
  a white pill — the white pill's problem wasn't the treatment in the abstract, it was contrast:
  against this photo's light sand it nearly disappeared, where a saturated wine pill holds up
  against sand, water and photo alike. The scrim was widened to match — content sitting at the
  vertical center needs coverage well past the old 62%-up cutoff, not just the bottom sliver.

  Third pass, same day: The owner asked for the eyebrow gone (the pass above had already removed it in
  the shared checkout, but not in the branch his preview was serving) and for the copy to lean
  summer. The headline the second pass landed on — "קיץ פורח" — was summery, but it stripped the
  page's only h1 of both flowers and Haifa, and per CLAUDE.md the homepage *is* the Haifa page.
  So the season stays and the place comes back: "קיץ פורח בחיפה". `פורח` carries the פרח root, so
  the h1 signals bloom, season and city in three short words without reading as a keyword list,
  and the h2 in florista-seo-copy still holds the literal "פרחים בחיפה" query.

  A supporting line was added under it rather than lengthening the h1 further. It carries the two
  things the photo cannot say — that these are summer flowers, and that they arrive today — and it
  lets the h1 stay short enough to hold display scale at 320px. Both strings are section settings
  with the coded copy as the fallback, per the standing editable-content split.

  Rosh Hashana 2026 skin, 2026-08-25, designed with the owner. Photo swapped to his
  `Hero_RoshHasanda_2026.jpg` (source preserved as `docs/brand/photography/hero-rosh-hashana-2026.
  jpg`, 5504×3072): a holiday table — bouquet, pomegranates and a honey jar in focus, family
  blurred behind, calm warm wall on the physical right. Same geometry as the beach photo (subject
  left, quiet space right), so the existing crop biases carry over. Headline is the classic
  "שנה טובה ומתוקה" (his longer greeting wrapped to three display lines at 375px, so it moved to
  the supporting line, corrected from ולמשפחתם to ולמשפחתכם — second person). CTA goes honey-gold
  via the `festive` setting — the owner asked for a חגיגי colour; honey echoes the jar in frame and
  the שנה מתוקה wish, and stays distinct from the warning amber (see tokens). CTA target is
  `/collections/rosh-hashana` — the collection is being created separately; the link 404s until
  it exists, acceptable only while the store is password-protected.

  Photo swapped again 2026-08-26 to the owner's `Hero_Rosh_Hasana New.png` (source preserved as
  `docs/brand/photography/hero-rosh-hashana-2026-v2.png`, 1088×608): a livelier take on the same
  table — three generations laughing, round challah, kiddush cup, pomegranates and honey, bouquet
  sharp front-left, same quiet wall on the physical right, so both crop biases carry over again.
  The source was native 1088px wide; on 2026-08-26 it was upscaled 4× with Real-ESRGAN
  (realesrgan-x4plus) at the owner's request and the ladder regenerated from that master —
  `hero-rosh2-{640,960,1280,1920,2560}.{jpg,webp}`, 4K master archived as
  `docs/brand/photography/hero-rosh-hashana-2026-v2-4k.jpg` (3840×2146). Faces are slightly
  painterly at 100% crop but sit in the photo's own soft-focus zone. Previous derivatives
  `hero-rosh-*` stay in assets for revert.

  2026-09-12: the <picture> moved out to snippets/florista-hero-image.liquid so the layout can
  preload the same image in <head> (Lighthouse mobile: LCP 3.4 s, 70% of it discovery delay).
  The image is now a theme setting with the committed seasonal ladder as fallback — weekly
  promotion swaps happen in the editor, not in this file.

  Fall 2026 skin, 2026-09-23, from the owner's reference (eyebrow / headline / one line / button,
  "well adjusted to Hebrew"). Fallback ladder is now hero-fall-* (bouquet, floral vase and a
  steaming tea on a wooden table — subject left, calm wall right, so both crop biases carry
  over again). Two schema changes: an optional eyebrow label above the headline, hidden when
  blank; and the `festive` checkbox became a `cta_skin` select — wine / honey (חגים) / cinnamon
  (סתיו) — because a checkbox cannot hold a third colour. CTA points at /collections/fall, a
  collection that is being created next; the link 404s until it exists. That target lives in
  the Liquid `default:` and in index.json only: Shopify rejects a `url` setting whose schema
  default is a store-specific path ("default must be a string or datasource access path" —
  the upload fails and the dev server serves 500), so the schema default stays /collections/all.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'florista-hero.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow
  assign title = section.settings.title | default: 'סתיו פורח בפלוריסטה'
  assign subtitle = section.settings.subtitle | default: 'זרים חדשים בגוונים החמים של העונה'
  assign cta_label = section.settings.cta_label | default: 'לזרי הסתיו'
  assign cta_url = section.settings.cta_url | default: '/collections/fall'
  assign cta_skin = section.settings.cta_skin | default: 'fall'
-%}

<section class="hero-full">
  {%- comment -%}
    The photo, its srcset ladder and its alt live in snippets/florista-hero-image.liquid and
    are chosen in theme settings ("פלוריסטה — באנר ראשי"), not here: the same snippet emits a
    <link rel="preload"> for this exact image in <head>, which a section cannot reach. Changing
    the image anywhere but there silently breaks the preload. 2026-09-12.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'florista-hero-image', mode: 'picture' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    No scrim since 2026-09-23. The owner, comparing the page with his original: "i hate the fact
    you make it darker". The photo shows at full brightness; legibility comes from WHERE the
    text sits (over the bright empty wall) and from ink-coloured type, not from shading.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  <div class="hero-content">
    {%- comment -%}
      h2, not h1: the hero headline is seasonal/editable, while the homepage's
      one h1 is the head term in the SEO copy section (seo-geo-haifa — the
      homepage owns פרחים בחיפה, and the crawlable heading must not rotate
      away with a campaign). Styling is class-based, so the tag carries no
      visual change at all.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <h2 class="hero-title">{{ title }}</h2>
    {%- if subtitle != blank -%}
      <p class="hero-subtitle">{{ subtitle }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <a class="hero-cta{% if cta_skin == 'festive' %} hero-cta--festive{% elsif cta_skin == 'fall' %} hero-cta--fall{% endif %}" href="{{ cta_url }}">{{ cta_label }}</a>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Florista hero",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "התמונה נבחרת בהגדרות ערכת העיצוב ← «פלוריסטה — באנר ראשי», כדי שהדפדפן יטען אותה ראשונה."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "תווית קטנה מעל הכותרת",
      "info": "שורה קצרה, למשל שם הקמפיין. ריק = בלי תווית.",
      "default": "קולקציית סתיו חדשה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "כותרת",
      "default": "סתיו פורח בפלוריסטה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "label": "כותרת משנה",
      "default": "זרים חדשים בגוונים החמים של העונה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "טקסט הכפתור",
      "default": "לזרי הסתיו"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_url",
      "label": "קישור הכפתור",
      "default": "/collections/all"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "cta_skin",
      "label": "צבע הכפתור",
      "info": "צבע עונתי לכפתור. יין הוא צבע המותג הרגיל.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "default", "label": "יין (רגיל)" },
        { "value": "festive", "label": "זהב־דבש (חגים)" },
        { "value": "fall", "label": "קינמון (סתיו)" }
      ],
      "default": "fall"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Florista hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
